From f8c8b0aecbdc9d9ccb721c6a8d86bd03c2a6b87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:21:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Keep fusion orchestration inside the target app lifecycle

Bind immutable persist-backed configuration during application startup, schedule bounded manifest and class-loader work, write through app-private storage, and suppress only explicitly authorized target ANR kills.

Constraint: Output stays under the target application external-files directory and ANR protection is exact-match, transactional, and disabled by default.

Rejected: Adding a broker service or shared storage writer | it expands privilege and duplicates existing process ownership.

Confidence: high

Scope-risk: moderate

Directive: Preserve fail-closed configuration and fail-open ANR behavior for invalid or non-target snapshots.

Tested: ANR source contract 1/1; git diff --cached --check; prior framework-minus-apex and services.core build; CoolApk protected 3/3 with disabled control.

Not-tested: Full FrameworksServicesTests remains blocked by pre-existing LockPatternUtils call-site compilation errors.
Change-Id: Icdbe21d4126be8aa9922213ea920295de3c1b54a
